# cloudflare
.open-next/
.wrangler/
# worker-configuration.d.ts IS committed. It is generated by `wrangler types`, but
# committing it keeps lint and typecheck reproducible: with the real Cloudflare runtime
# types present, several type assertions become unnecessary and ESLint errors on them,
# so a tree without this file lints differently from one with it. It holds binding
# names and types only, no ids or secrets. Regenerate with `npm run cf:typegen` after
# changing wrangler.jsonc.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Internal working material. Present in the working copy, absent from the repo.
#
# None of this is secret and none of it is deleted: it is the scaffolding a
# reader of this project does not need and in two cases should not receive.
# What is durable in it was rewritten into README.md and docs/, which are the
# public documentation.
#
#   Agent instructions and process   The working agreements, the enforced
#                                    conventions, the reflection ledger, and a
#                                    review tool's output. Meaningless outside
#                                    the sessions that produced them.
#
#   Specs                            SPEC.md and BUILD_SPEC.md are written to a
#                                    hackathon brief and carry its deadlines,
#                                    prize and Discord threads, plus a running
#                                    decision log that reads as contradiction
#                                    without the history. docs/architecture.md
#                                    and docs/data-model.md carry what lasts.
#
#   Competitor material              40 screenshots of Sessionboard's own UI and
#                                    the control-by-control transcriptions taken
#                                    off them. Someone else's product; it stays
#                                    out of a public repository.
#
#   Hackathon and eval artifacts     Brief snapshots, Discord logs, a video
#                                    transcript, evaluation runs and the design
#                                    documents behind individual features.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

